<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Democratic-Republican Party</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1792–1825</span> · Also known as Jeffersonian Republicans</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Democratic-Republican Party was an American political party founded in the early 1790s by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-jefferson">Thomas Jefferson</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-madison">James Madison</a> in opposition to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-hamilton">Alexander Hamilton</a>'s Federalists. Favouring states' rights, agrarian interests and a strict reading of the Constitution, it held the presidency from 1801 to 1825 and then split into factions, from one of which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/democratic-party-united-states">Democratic Party</a> emerged.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/democratic-republican-party.jpg" alt="Democratic-Republican Party" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Angelus · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tricolour_Cockade.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
